course: dictionary
lesson: 12985
title: Expend: using up energy, time and money
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Expend is a formal word. It means to use or spend something, such as energy, time, effort or money. «Ben expended a lot of energy running up the hill.» Ben did not just run. He used up a lot of his energy doing it.
explain: The second meaning is stronger. To expend something can mean to use it up completely. «The battery was expended by the end of the game.» Nothing is left in the battery now. Read the words around expend to find out which meaning fits.
explain: You can often swap in a simpler word to check. «We expended all our money on a new bike» means we spent all our money on a new bike. If the sentence still makes sense with spent or used up, your meaning is right.
fact: Expend means to use or spend energy, time, effort or money.
fact: Expend is a formal word, so you will see it more in writing than in chatting.
fact: «Expend energy» and «expend effort» are common phrases.
fact: «Expended» means used up, and it tells you that something is now gone or greatly reduced.
fact: Spent is a simpler word you can use instead of expend in many sentences, as in «She spent her last coin».
exercise: «Ben expended a lot of energy running up the hill.» What does expended mean here? | Saved for later | Forgot about | *Used up, spent | Found again
exercise: Which phrase means the same as «expend effort»? | Gain effort | Lose a hat | Eat lunch | *Use up effort
exercise: «The battery was expended by the end of the game.» What has happened to the battery? | It has been painted | It has been charged | It has been dropped | *It has been used up
test: «He expended all his time on the project.» Which word is closest in meaning to expended? | Lent | Saved | Stopped | *Spent
test: Which word could replace expended in «She expended her last coin on a bus ticket»? | *Spent | Sang | Hid | Found
exam: «The scientists expended great effort to finish the experiment, and the results were clear.» What does expended show? | Effort was never needed | *Effort was used up | Effort was found in a box | Effort was given away to others
